# Patches must stay LF on checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# These are applied with `git apply` to a freshly cloned ghostty tree, which is
# LF. With autocrlf=true — the default on this machine — a fresh clone of this
# repo would hand them out with CRLF endings and `git apply` would reject them,
# on a checkout where nothing looks wrong and the files were never edited. The
# in-repo bytes are already LF; this is about what lands in the working tree.
*.patch -text
*.diff -text

# Same reasoning: the WASM comparison binaries and any other binary artifacts
# must never be line-ending translated.
*.wasm binary
